{"nodes": [{"id": "doxygen_documentation_manuals_ros_manual_ros_manual_ros", "label": "Chrono::ROS reference manual", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "doxygen/documentation/manuals/ros/manual_ros.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "doxygen_documentation_manuals_ros_manual_ros_schema_driven_bridge", "label": "Schema-driven bridge (Chrono 10.0 change)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "doxygen/documentation/manuals/ros/manual_ros.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A message type is now identified by its ROS type-name string and serialized to/from CDR by Chrono itself over shared memory, so the ROS subprocess is generic and no longer compiled per message type. Built-in handlers keep their interfaces, but a custom handler written against the old design must be rewritten - the payoff is no IPC struct, no message-type enum, no subprocess file and no Chrono rebuild, plus custom handlers in Python."}, {"id": "doxygen_documentation_manuals_ros_manual_ros_process_separation", "label": "ROS node process separation (Chrono 9.0 change)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "doxygen/documentation/manuals/ros/manual_ros.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The ROS 2 node was moved into a separate process connected over shared memory specifically to resolve and prevent symbol collisions between the ROS 2 and Chrono process spaces; the schema-driven bridge retains this separation."}], "edges": [{"source": "doxygen_documentation_manuals_ros_manual_ros_manual_ros", "target": "doxygen_documentation_manuals_ros_ros_overview_chrono_ros", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "doxygen/documentation/manuals/ros/manual_ros.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}